Workqueue monitor: skip threads whose /proc/<tid>/stat cannot be opened.

What: the thread pool monitor counts runnable workers by reading
/proc/<tid>/stat; an open() failure was a DISPATCH_CLIENT_CRASH. The thread is
now simply not counted as running.
Why: without procfs (or with a flaky one, as on iSH) this is a silent SIGTRAP.
Upstream: likely acceptable.

Apply inside the `swift-corelibs-libdispatch` repository: git apply <this file>
---
diff --git a/src/event/workqueue.c b/src/event/workqueue.c
--- a/src/event/workqueue.c
+++ b/src/event/workqueue.c
@@ -162,8 +162,11 @@
 
 		fd = open(path, O_RDONLY | O_NONBLOCK);
 		if (unlikely(fd == -1)) {
-			DISPATCH_CLIENT_CRASH(tid,
-					"workq: registered worker exited prematurely");
+			// procfs may be missing or unreliable (containers without /proc,
+			// sandboxes, emulators): treat the worker as not runnable
+			// instead of crashing the process.
+			_dispatch_debug("workq: Failed to open %s", path);
+			continue;
 		} else {
 			bytes_read = read(fd, buf, sizeof(buf)-1);
 			(void)close(fd);
